    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Здрасте.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hello.' Elena offers a very casual, shortened greeting as she arrives at the apartment early in the morning.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Доброе утро.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Good morning.' Elena follows up with a standard morning greeting.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Это Макс?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Is this Max?' She wants to make sure she is talking to the right person.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Да, это я.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, it is me.' Max confirms his identity using a simple phrase that directly connects the word for this with himself.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Я ищу его.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am looking for him.' Elena states her purpose immediately, using a single action word to explain she is trying to find the Chef.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Дома не могу ему дозвониться.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'At home I can't reach him.' Elena explains her early visit by noting she could not reach him by phone at his own place.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Где он?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Where is he?' Elena demands to know his location with a blunt, one-word question.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Я не знаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I don't know.' Max answers honestly that he has no idea where his roommate is.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Наверное, ключи висят.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Probably, the keys are hanging.' Max notices the keys are on the hook, guessing that this means the Chef has not left.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Значит, он дома.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'So, he is home.' Max concludes logically that the Chef must be around, linking the word for means directly to at home.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Вы хотите войти?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do you want to come in?' Max politely asks if she would like to step inside, raising his voice at the end of the sentence to form the question.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Проходите.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Come in.' Max invites her to enter by using a direct, formal request. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
